#' Example ASR table from canregtools
#'
#' A sample age-standardized rate (ASR) table generated by a
#' `canregtools::create_asr()` workflow and labelled by
#' `canregtools::add_labels()`. The dataset is used as an example input for
#' text generation functions such as [cr_overview()].
#'
#' @format An object of class `asr`, `tbl_df`, `tbl`, and `data.frame` with
#' 4956 rows and 19 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{areacode}{Area code.}
#'   \item{areacode_en}{Area label in English.}
#'   \item{areacode_cn}{Area label in Chinese.}
#'   \item{year}{Calendar year.}
#'   \item{sex}{Sex code: 0 for total, 1 for male, and 2 for female.}
#'   \item{sex_en}{Sex label in English.}
#'   \item{sex_cn}{Sex label in Chinese.}
#'   \item{cancer}{Cancer site code.}
#'   \item{cancer_en}{Cancer site label in English.}
#'   \item{cancer_cn}{Cancer site label in Chinese.}
#'   \item{no_cases}{Number of cases or deaths.}
#'   \item{cr}{Crude rate per 100,000 population.}
#'   \item{asr_cn2000}{Age-standardized rate using the China 2000 standard population.}
#'   \item{asr_wld85}{Age-standardized rate using Segi's world standard population.}
#'   \item{truncr_cn2000}{Truncated China 2000 age-standardized rate.}
#'   \item{truncr_wld85}{Truncated world age-standardized rate.}
#'   \item{cumur}{Cumulative rate.}
#'   \item{prop}{Proportion among all malignant tumors.}
#'   \item{rank}{Rank among cancer sites within each area, year, and sex stratum.}
#' }
#'
#' @source Generated from a `canregtools` ASR workflow.
"asr"

#' Example age-specific rate table from canregtools
